  status: smoke
description: 'v028''s exact recipe with the ONE axis that has never been varied: the
  MLP head width. model.head_hidden 192 -> 384, so 225,922 -> 263,362 params (+16.5%).
  The recurrent trunk is untouched at hidden 128.'
hypothesis: "The reasoning is that v028 finishes in 46m52s of a 60-minute budget,\
  \ so 14 minutes are unspent, and capacity is the obvious thing to spend them on.\
  \ That reasoning is right about the headroom and WRONG about which part to enlarge,\
  \ and the distinction is the whole point of this run.\nPer-row compute splits as:\
  \ GRU1 44.0%, GRU0 33.0%, head 16.7%, projection 6.4%. So the recurrent trunk is\
  \ 83.3% of the cost and the head is 16.7%. Every capacity experiment we have run\
  \ spent on the trunk, and all of them lost:\n  hidden 128 -> 285 (871,977 params):\
  \ -2.2 sigma, and TIMED OUT on the grader\n  hidden 128 -> 415 (1,742,717 params):\
  \ -10.2 sigma, and TIMED OUT\nWidening the trunk does not merely fail to help, it\
  \ fails twice and costs the submission outright. dozken's own data agrees: his 384x2\
  \ teacher was +0.003 over 192x2, and his 872k scored the same as 436k.\nThe head\
  \ has NEVER been varied, so it is the only place where \"bigger\" is both affordable\
  \ and untested. Doubling it adds 16.5% compute against the trunk's 83.3%, so the\
  \ grader projection moves from 78% of budget to roughly 86% -- still inside the\
  \ limit, unlike the trunk changes which blew straight through it.\nPrediction, and\
  \ it is genuinely uncertain in a way the trunk runs were not: a wider readout may\
  \ help, may do nothing, or may hurt. The trunk results give a reason to expect harm,\
  \ since they suggest extra capacity in this problem is absorbed as overfitting rather\
  \ than used. The counter is that the head is a different KIND of capacity -- it\
  \ is where the t0/t1 readouts are formed, it consumes the skip from the 64-wide\
  \ projection, and no trunk experiment ever touched it. If this returns within 0.000317\
  \ of v028 then head width is not a lever either, and combined with the trunk results\
  \ that closes capacity as an axis entirely. If it returns worse by more than 0.000317,\
  \ that is consistent and expected."
change_vs_parent: 'model.head_hidden 192 -> 384, and the script change that plumbs
  model.head_hidden through BOTH model construction sites (training and export) so
  train and serve cannot diverge. Verified: with no head_hidden key the constructor
  reproduces v028''s 225,922 params exactly, so the plumbing itself is a no-op for
  every other run. hidden, input_proj, layers, dropout, distill_weight, gamma, chunk_len,
  epochs, teacher, schedule, LR and seed are all unchanged.'
